  "registerPolicy": "Two spoken registers only: casual (nuvvu, -av endings) and respectful (meeru, -aru/-andi endings), in the standard spoken Telugu of Coastal Andhra. Written or formal-literary forms are out of scope. 'neutral' = the sentence has no you-form, so no register choice is needed. Casual items may end in ra (male friend) or ve (female friend); `addressee` records which.",
